{%- import "macros.njk" as m with context -%}
<h1>Accessibility statement</h1>

<p class="lede">This site aims to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 at Level AA on every page and in every calculator. {% if a11y.status != "complete" %}The assessment is not complete, so we do not yet claim that it does.{% endif %}</p>

{% if a11y.status != "complete" %}
{% call m.note("Status: assessment not complete", 2, "status-assessment-not-complete") %}
<p>{% if not site.production %}This is a preview. {% endif %}An AI assistant has run automated checks and some scripted checks. The tests that need a person, and are not yet done, are listed under <a href="#not-tested">What has not been tested</a>. Automated checks alone cannot show that a site meets the guidelines. We will not describe the site as meeting WCAG 2.2 AA until every check below is done and every failure is fixed.</p>
{% endcall %}
{% endif %}

<h2 id="scope">What this statement covers</h2>
<p>Every page of this site and the four calculators, in their normal state, with an error showing, with details opened and after a result has changed.</p>

<h2 id="how-to-use">What you should be able to do</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Use every page and calculator with a keyboard alone.</li>
  <li>See where keyboard focus is at all times.</li>
  <li>Zoom to 400% without losing content or scrolling sideways, except inside wide tables and charts, which scroll on their own.</li>
  <li>Read every chart as a table. No information depends on colour alone.</li>
  <li>Use the site in a light or dark colour scheme, following your device's setting.</li>
  <li>Read every explanation with JavaScript switched off. The calculators need JavaScript. Each shows a worked example or a default result without it.</li>
  <li>Enter figures by typing. No calculator needs dragging or a slider.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="tested">What has been tested</h2>
{% if a11y.done | length %}
{#- When every test shares one environment and date, say so once. -#}
{%- set runs = [] %}
{%- for item in a11y.done %}{% set key = item.environment ~ item.date %}{% if key not in runs %}{% set _ = runs.push(key) %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
{%- set oneRun = (runs | length) == 1 %}
{% if oneRun %}<p>Every test below used {{ a11y.done[0].environment }} They ran on {{ a11y.done[0].date | timeTag | safe }}.</p>{% endif %}
<dl>
  {%- for item in a11y.done %}
  <dt>{{ item.check }}</dt> <dd>{{ item.result }}{% if not oneRun %} {{ item.environment }} Tested on {{ item.date | timeTag | safe }}.{% endif %}</dd>
  {%- endfor %}
</dl>
{% else %}
<p>No test results are recorded yet.</p>
{% endif %}

<h2 id="not-tested">What has not been tested</h2>
{% if a11y.not_done | length %}
<dl>
  {%- for item in a11y.not_done %}
  <dt>{{ item.check }}</dt> <dd>{{ item.reason }}</dd>
  {%- endfor %}
</dl>
{% else %}
<p>Nothing is recorded as outstanding.</p>
{% endif %}

<h2 id="known-issues">Known problems</h2>
{% if a11y.known_issues | length %}
<dl>
  {%- for item in a11y.known_issues %}
  <dt>{{ item.issue }}</dt> <dd>{{ item.detail }} WCAG {{ item.criterion }}.</dd>
  {%- endfor %}
</dl>
{% else %}
<p>No failure found in testing is still open. That covers only the tests listed above.</p>
{% endif %}

<h2 id="report">Report a problem</h2>
{% if site.correctionUrl %}
<p>If you cannot use part of this site, <a href="{{ site.correctionUrl }}">tell us what you were trying to do and what happened</a>.</p>
{%- if site.correctionUrl.startsWith("https://github.com/") %}
<p>The link opens a new issue on GitHub, the website that holds this site's source files. It is the only way to report a problem: there is no email address. You need a GitHub account to send a report. It is free, but it is still a barrier, and it is a known limit of this site.</p>
{%- endif %}
{% else %}
{% call m.unavailable("a way to report a problem", 3, "not-available-a-way-to-report-a-problem") %}
<p>The route for reporting a problem has not been set up. This is one of the decisions to make before the site is published. The site will not be published without it.</p>
{% endcall %}
{% endif %}

<h2 id="dates">Preparation of this statement</h2>
<p>{% if a11y.assessed_on %}The recorded date of the tests listed is {{ a11y.assessed_on | timeTag | safe }}.{% else %}No assessment date is recorded.{% endif %} The full assessment, criterion by criterion, is kept with the site's source files.</p>
